desc:GFX G Fool [arp synth]
//tags: instrument synth arpeggiator generative sequencer arcana
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument and gfx-voice (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE FOOL (card 0 of the GFX Arcana series): the beginning of the journey. A self-contained synth with
// THREE ARPEGGIATORS - three paths - fed by the same held chord. Each path has its own pattern length, so paths
// of different lengths drift in and out of phase and the whole figure only repeats after the least common
// multiple of their lengths.
//   PATH I / II / III   ON; MODE up / down / up-down / random (a fixed random order, repeats every LENGTH steps) /
//                       as played / chord; RATE (1/2 - 1/32, dotted and triplet, locked to the project tempo);
//                       LENGTH (2-16 steps); OCTAVES (1-4); OFFSET (-2..+2 octaves); GATE; SWING; PROB (step chance)
//                       and its own voice, in the world of the early minimalists' combo and electric organs:
//                       SQUARE (combo-organ pulse; WIDTH narrows it, thin and reedy), TRI (transistor triangle; EDGE folds
//                       in a buzz) or ORGAN (drawbars 8' + 4' + 2 2/3' + 2', BARS pulls them out; a touch of leakage, key
//                       click and percussion), CUTOFF and RESO (12 dB low-pass with key tracking), DECAY (plucky to HOLD:
//                       fully up the note sustains for its gate, organ-like), LEVEL, PAN and SEND (to MD-6 and the plate)
//   LFO (one per path)  SHAPE sine / triangle / saw / square / S&H / smooth random; DESTINATION cutoff / reso / decay /
//                       level / pan / send; RATE synced (4 bars - 1/16) or free (0.02 - 20 Hz); DEPTH +/-; RETRIG
//   STEP OFF            throws all three paths into a fresh pattern: MODE, LENGTH, OFFSET and PROB are re-dealt within
//                       musical limits from a SEED (shown on the display; the same seed always deals the same hand).
//                       RETURN swaps back to the pattern before (press again to step off to it once more).
//                       The mouse wheel on the SEED display deals seed by seed; a click on it opens a list (a random
//                       seed, the seeds either side, jumps by the hundred).
//   HOLD                latch: the chord stays until a new one is played.  KEY SYNC restarts the patterns on every
//                       new chord (on the next step of the grid); FREE keeps them locked to the song position.
//   TRANSPOSE, SCALE (off / major / minor / dorian / pentatonic) and ROOT keep random patterns in key.
//   THE JOURNEY         CF-1  the Ten Rack's chorus / flanger pedal, an insert on the dry paths (the organ's shimmer):
//                             MORPH, RATE, DEPTH, MANUAL, REGEN, ON
//                       MD-6  the Ten Rack's modulated delay on the paths' SENDs, with tempo SYNC (1/16 - 1 bar) or free
//                             time (20 ms - 2 s): TIME, FEEDBACK, LEVEL, WOW (rate), DEPTH, ON - the tape-echo canon
//                       PLATE the Platte81's West plate with its Vocal Plate settings, fed by the sends and the echoes:
//                             DECAY, PRE (delay), MIX, ON
//   FATE (the series' drift, 0-100 %, 50 % = the standard amount): the cards reshuffle a little - each path's
//                       micro-timing, step chance, filter cutoff and pan wander slowly and independently; the tuning
//                       wanders a touch and every note lands slightly differently in tune.
//   VOLUME and SAT (the output soft clip is always on).
// Tempo-locked when the project plays, free-running from the first key when stopped. Notes are timed inside the
// synth (each note carries its own gate), so chord changes or a transport stop never leave a note hanging.
// MIDI: notes (channel select), CC120 / CC123 all notes off.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc

slider1:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-I on
slider2:0<0,5,1{Up,Down,Up-Down,Random,As played,Chord}>-I mode
slider3:4<0,10,1{1/2,1/4,1/4D,1/4T,1/8,1/8D,1/8T,1/16,1/16D,1/16T,1/32}>-I rate
slider4:6<2,16,1>-I length (steps)
slider5:1<1,4,1>-I octaves
slider6:0<-2,2,1>-I octave offset
slider7:80<10,100,1>-I gate (%)
slider8:0<0,75,1>-I swing (%)
slider9:100<0,100,1>-I probability (%)
slider10:2<0,2,1{Square,Triangle,Organ}>-I wave
slider11:6000<80,16000,1>-I cutoff (Hz)
slider12:10<0,100,1>-I resonance (%)
slider13:5000<20,5000,1>-I decay (ms, 5000 = hold)
slider14:70<0,100,1>-I level (%)
